hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28184","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Shuayb, on the authority of Umm Kurz al-Khuzaiyyah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a boy and he urinated on him, and he ordered with it and it was sprinkled, and a girl was brought and she urinated on him, and he ordered with it and it was washed."
"28185","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Umarah, on the authority of Abu al-Shatha, he said: I went out for Hajj and came until I entered the House, and when I was between the two pillars I went until I clung to the wall. Ibn Umar came and prayed beside me, and he prayed four. When he prayed, I said: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray of the House? He said: Usamah ibn Zayd informed me that he prayed here. I said: How many did he pray? He said: On this I find myself blaming myself, I remained with him a lifetime and did not ask him how many he prayed. Then I performed Hajj the next year and came and stood in his standing place, and Ibn al-Zubayr came and prayed in it four."
